<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6633" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">căpĭto</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>amplif.</i>
			[caput], <i>one that has a large head</i>, <i>big-headed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 29, 80</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A sea-fish with a large head</i>, <i>called also</i> cephalus, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
				158, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A kind of fish with a large head</i>: Cyprinus
			dobula, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Aus. Mos. 85</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>